I 툴","개발 툴"],"es":["Vercel React","Agentes de IA","Mejores prácticas de Vercel","Cómo usar Vercel con React","Alternativas a Vercel","Guía de instalación de Vercel","Configuración de Vercel React","Optimización de rendimiento en Vercel"],"fr":["Vercel React","Outils d''IA","Bonnes pratiques Vercel","Comment utiliser Vercel avec React","Alternatives à Vercel","Guide d''installation de Vercel","Configuration de Vercel React","Optimisation des performances dans Vercel"],"de":["Vercel React","KI-Agenten","Vercel Best Practices","Wie man Vercel mit React verwendet","Alternativen zu Vercel","Vercel-Installationsanleitung","Vercel-React-Konfiguration","Leistungsoptimierung in Vercel"],"pt":["como usar Vercel com React","o que é um plugin de workflow de IA","melhores práticas de desenvolvimento web","Vercel vs Netlify","instalar plugin de workflow de IA","guias de configuração de Vercel","desenvolvimento de aplicativos web escaláveis","ferramentas de desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["как использовать Vercel с React","что такое плагин рабочего процесса ИИ","лучшие практики веб-разработки","Vercel vs Netlify","установка плагина рабочего процесса ИИ","руководства по настройке Vercel","разработка масштабируемых веб-приложений","инструменты веб-разработки"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام فركل مع رياكت","ما هي إضافة تدفق العمل الذكية","أفضل الممارسات لتطوير الويب","فركل مقابل نيتليفي","تثبيت إضافة تدفق العمل الذكية","دلائل إعداد فركل","تطوير تطبيقات الويب القابلة للتوسيع","أدوات تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"CloudAI-X","repo":"claude-workflow-v2","repoPath":"CloudAI-X/claude-workflow-v2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.886Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vercel-react-best-practices","description":"React and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering. This skill should be used when writing, reviewing, or refactoring React/Next.js code to ensure optimal performance patterns. Triggers on tasks involving React components, Next.js pages, data fetching, bundle optimization, or performance improvements.","bodyPreview":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\n### When to Load\n\n- **Trigger**: React or Next.js development, component writing, data fetching patterns, bundle optimization\n- **Skip**: Project does not use React or Next.js\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 45 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Writing new React com","body":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\n### When to Load\n\n- **Trigger**: React or Next.js development, component writing, data fetching patterns, bundle optimization\n- **Skip**: Project does not use React or Next.js\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 45 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Writing new React components or Next.js pages\n- Implementing data fetching (client or server-side)\n- Reviewing code for performance issues\n- Refactoring existing React/Next.js code\n- Optimizing bundle size or load times\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category                  | Impact      | Prefix       |\n| -------- | ------------------------- | ----------- | ------------ |\n| 1        | Eliminating Waterfalls    | CRITICAL    | `async-`     |\n| 2        | Bundle Size Optimization  | CRITICAL    | `bundle-`    |\n| 3        | Server-Side Performance   | HIGH        | `server-`    |\n| 4        | Client-Side Data Fetching | MEDIUM-HIGH | `client-`    |\n| 5        | Re-render Optimization    | MEDIUM      | `rerender-`  |\n| 6        | Rendering Performance     | MEDIUM      | `rendering-` |\n| 7        | JavaScript Performance    | LOW-MEDIUM  | `js-`        |\n| 8        | Advanced Patterns         | LOW         | `advanced-`  |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### 1. Eliminating Waterfalls (CRITICAL)\n\n- `async-defer-await` - Move await into branches where actually used\n- `async-parallel` - Use Promise.all() for independent operations\n- `async-dependencies` - Use better-all for partial dependencies\n- `async-api-routes` - Start promises early, await late in API routes\n- `async-suspense-boundaries` - Use Suspense to stream content\n\n### 2. Bundle Size Optimization (CRITICAL)\n\n- `bundle-barrel-imports` - Import directly, avoid barrel files\n- `bundle-dynamic-imports` - Use next/dynamic for heavy components\n- `bundle-defer-third-party` - Load analytics/logging after hydration\n- `bundle-conditional` - Load modules only when feature is activated\n- `bundle-preload` - Preload on hover/focus for perceived speed\n\n### 3. Server-Side Performance (HIGH)\n\n- `server-cache-react` - Use React.cache() for per-request deduplication\n- `server-cache-lru` - Use LRU cache for cross-request caching\n- `server-serialization` - Minimize data passed to client components\n- `server-parallel-fetching` - Restructure components to parallelize fetches\n- `server-after-nonblocking` - Use after() for non-blocking operations\n\n### 4. Client-Side Data Fetching (MEDIUM-HIGH)\n\n- `client-swr-dedup` - Use SWR for automatic request deduplication\n- `client-event-listeners` - Deduplicate global event listeners\n\n### 5. Re-render Optimization (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rerender-defer-reads` - Don''t subscribe to state only used in callbacks\n- `rerender-memo` - Extract expensive work into memoized components\n- `rerender-dependencies` - Use primitive dependencies in effects\n- `rerender-derived-state` - Subscribe to derived booleans, not raw values\n- `rerender-functional-setstate` - Use functional setState for stable callbacks\n- `rerender-lazy-state-init` - Pass function to useState for expensive values\n- `rerender-transitions` - Use startTransition for non-urgent updates\n\n### 6. Rendering Performance (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rendering-animate-svg-wrapper` - Animate div wrapper, not SVG element\n- `rendering-content-visibility` - Use content-visibility for long lists\n- `rendering-hoist-jsx` - Extract static JSX outside components\n- `rendering-svg-precision` - Reduce SVG coordinate precision\n- `rendering-hydration-no-flicker` - Use inline script for client-only data\n- `rendering-activity` - Use Activity component for show/hide\n- `rendering-conditional-render` - Use ternary, not && for conditionals\n\n### 7. JavaScript Performance (LOW-MEDIUM)\n\n- `js-batch-dom-css` - Group CSS changes via classes or cssText\n- `js-index-maps` - Build Map for repeated lookups\n- `js-cache-property-access` - Cache object properties in loops\n- `js-cache-function-results` - Cache function results in module-level Map\n- `js-cache-storage` - Cache localStorage/sessionStorage reads\n- `js-combine-iterations` - Combine multiple filter/map into one loop\n- `js-length-check-first` - Check array length before expensive comparison\n- `js-early-exit` - Return early from functions\n- `js-hoist-regexp` - Hoist RegExp creation outside loops\n- `js-min-max-loop` - Use loop for min/max instead of sort\n- `js-set-map-lookups` - Use Set/Map for O(1) lookups\n- `js-tosorted-immutable` - Use toSorted() for immutability\n\n### 8. Advanced Patterns (LOW)\n\n- `advanced-event-handler-refs` - Store event handlers in refs\n- `advanced-use-latest` - useLatest for stable callback refs\n\n## Full Compiled Document\n\nFor the complete guide with all rules expanded and detailed code examples, see: `AGENTS.md`\n\nEach rule contains:\n\n- Brief explanation of why it matters\n- Incorrect code example with explanation\n- Correct code example with explanation\n- Additional context and references\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:09:09.448Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents focusing on React and Next.js development, seeking to optimize performance and follow best practices","zh":"非常适合专注于React和Next.js开发的前端代理，寻求优化性能和遵循最佳实践","ja":"ReactとNext.jsの開発に重点を置くフロントエンドエージェントに最適で、パフォーマンスを最適化し、ベストプラクティスに従うことを目指している","ko":"React와 Next.js 개발에 중점을 둔 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합하며, 성능을 최적화하고 최선의 관행을 따르는 것을 목표로 하는 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Frontend que se centran en el desarrollo de React y Next.js, y que buscan optimizar el rendimiento y seguir las mejores prácticas","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui se concentrent sur le développement React et Next.js, et qui cherchent à optimiser les performances et à suivre les meilleures pratiques","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die sich auf die Entwicklung von React und Next.js konzentrieren und die Leistung optimieren und die besten Praktiken befolgen möchten","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que se concentram no desenvolvimento de React e Next.js, buscando otimizar o desempenho e seguir as melhores práticas","ru":"Идеально подходит для фронтенд-агентов, специализирующихся на разработке React и Next.js, стремящихся оптимизировать производительность и следовать лучшим практикам","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم التي تركز على تطوير React و Next.js، سعياً لتحسين الأداء اتباع أفضل الممارسات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate refactoring and code generation for React and Next.js applications using Vercel''s comprehensive performance optimization guide, covering 45 rules across 8 categories, including bundle optimization and data fetching patterns","zh":"赋予代理人使用Vercel的综合性能优化指南为React和Next.js应用程序自动化重构和代码生成的能力，涵盖45条规则，跨8个类别，包括包优化和数据获取模式","ja":"Vercelの包括的なパフォーマンス最適化ガイドを使用して、ReactとNext.jsアプリケーションに自動リファクタリングとコード生成を実行する機能をエージェントに与え、45のルールを8つのカテゴリにわたってカバーし、バンドル最適化とデータ取得パターンを含む","ko":"Vercel의 종합적 성능 최적화 가이드를 사용하여 React와 Next.js 애플리케이션에 자동 리팩토링 및 코드 생성을 수행하는 기능을 에이전트에게 부여하며, 45개의 규칙을 8개 범주에 걸쳐 다루며, 번들 최적화 및 데이터 가져오기 패턴을 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar la refactorización y la generación de código para aplicaciones React y Next.js utilizando la guía integral de optimización del rendimiento de Vercel, que cubre 45 reglas en 8 categorías, incluyendo la optimización de paquetes y los patrones de obtención de datos","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser la refactoring et la génération de code pour les applications React et Next.js en utilisant le guide complet d''optimisation des performances de Vercel, couvrant 45 règles dans 8 catégories, notamment l''optimisation des bundles et les modèles de récupération de données","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Refactoring und Codegenerierung für React- und Next.js-Anwendungen zu automatisieren, indem sie den umfassenden Leistungs-Optimierungsleitfaden von Vercel verwenden, der 45 Regeln in 8 Kategorien abdeckt, einschließlich Bundle-Optimierung und Datenabrufmuster","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a refatoração e a geração de código para aplicações React e Next.js usando o guia abrangente de otimização de desempenho da Vercel, que abrange 45 regras em 8 categorias, incluindo otimização de bundle e padrões de busca de dados","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать рефакторинг и генерацию кода для приложений React и Next.js с помощью всестороннего руководства Vercel по оптимизации производительности, охватывающего 45 правил в 8 категориях, включая оптимизацию пакета и шаблоны запроса данных","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تautomatizar إعادة هيكلة وتوليد الكود لتقديم React و Next.js باستخدام دليل شامل لتحسين الأداء من Vercel، الذي يغطي 45 قاعدة في 8 فئات، بما في ذلك تحسين الحزمة وأنماط استرجاع البيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for React components","Generating optimized code for Next.js pages","Debugging performance issues in React applications"],"zh":["自动化React组件的代码审查","为Next.js页面生成优化代码","调试React应用程序的性能问题"],"ja":["Reactコンポーネントのコードレビューを自動化する","Next.jsページの最適化コードを生成する","Reactアプリケーションのパフォーマンスの問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["React 컴포넌트의 코드 리뷰를 자동화","Next.js 페이지의 최적화 코드를 생성","React 애플리케이션의 성능 문제를 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar las revisiones de código para componentes React","Generar código optimizado para páginas Next.js","Depurar problemas de rendimiento en aplicaciones React"],"fr":["Automatiser les revues de code pour les composants React","Générer du code optimisé pour les pages Next.js","Déboguer les problèmes de performances dans les applications React"],"de":["Automatisieren von Code-Reviews für React-Komponenten","Generieren von optimiertem Code für Next.js-Seiten","Debuggen von Leistungsproblemen in React-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para componentes React","Gerar código otimizado para páginas Next.js","Depurar problemas de desempenho em aplicações React"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода для компонентов React","Генерировать оптимизированный код для страниц Next.js","Отладить проблемы производительности в приложениях React"],"ar":["توسيع مراجعة الكود التلقائي لمكونات React","توليد كود محسّن لأجزاء Next.js","تصحيح مشاكل الأداء في تطبيقات React"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React or Next.js project setup","Limited to React and Next.js frameworks"],"zh":["需要React或Next.js项目设置","仅限于React和Next.js框架"],"ja":["ReactまたはNext.jsプロジェクトの設定が必要","ReactとNext.jsフレームワークのみに限定"],"ko":["React 또는 Next.js 프로젝트 설정이 필요","React와 Next.js 프레임워크에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de proyecto React o Next.js","Limitado a los frameworks React y Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de projet React ou Next.js","Limité aux frameworks React et Next.js"],"de":["Benötigt React- oder Next.js-Projektsetup","Begrenzt auf React- und Next.js-Frameworks"],"pt":["Exige configuração do projeto React ou Next.js","Limitado aos quadros React e Next.js"],"ru":["Требует настройки проекта React или Next.js","Ограничен фреймворками React и Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مشروع React أو Next.js","محدود بإطارات العمل React و Next.js"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"4c0cd31ccfe6314b8209218baaf9e1721d08ee30955ff023d2e6cd48fde0e945","qualityScore":24}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('tachyon-zcash/ragu/book-review', 'community', 'tachyon-zcash', 'ragu', 'tachyon-zcash/ragu', 'book-review', 0, 0, 24, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.895Z', '2026-03-02T02:10:41.343Z', '03ecd3daf1c141683fc43f208d3e2aa567dcb6a2478d219704e3e6dbd58cc56e', '{"id":"tachyon-zcash/ragu/book-review","name":"book-review","description":{"zh":"Rust语言证明携带数据框架是一个用于构建安全可靠的数据处理系统的工具","ja":"Rust言語プルーフキャリングデータフレームワークは、安全かつ信頼性の高いデータ処理システムを構築するためのツールです","ko":"러스트 언어 증명携带 데이터 프레임워크는 안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 데이터 처리 시스템을 구축하기 위한 도구입니다","es":"El marco de datos de prueba de Rust es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite implementar pruebas de datos de manera eficiente","fr":"Le cadre de données de preuve de langage Rust est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de mettre en œuvre des tests de données de manière efficace","de":"Das Rust-Sprachframework für Datenprüfung ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das die effiziente Implementierung von Datenprüfungen ermöglicht","pt":"O framework de dados de prova de Rust é uma tecnologia de IA que permite aos desenvolvedores criar aplicativos mais seguros e eficientes.","ru":"Фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust - это технология ИИ, которая позволяет разработчикам создавать более безопасные и эффективные приложения.","ar":"إطار بيانات لغة روست هو تكنولوجيا ذكاء اصطناعي يسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تطبيقات أكثر أمانًا وكفاءة.","en":"Rust language proof-carrying data framework"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：Rust语言证明携带数据框架","ja":"AIエージェント：Rust言語プルーフキャリングデータフレームワーク","ko":"AI 에이전트: 러스트 언어 증명 携带 데이터 프레임워크","es":"Herramientas de AI: Marco de datos de prueba de Rust","fr":"Outils d''IA: Cadre de données de preuve de langage Rust","de":"KI-Tools: Rust-Sprachframework für Datenprüfung","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Framework de Dados de Prova de Rust","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: إطار بيانات لغة روست","en":"book-review"},"description":{"zh":"Rust语言证明携带数据框架是一个用于构建安全可靠的数据处理系统的工具","ja":"Rust言語プルーフキャリングデータフレームワークは、安全かつ信頼性の高いデータ処理システムを構築するためのツールです","ko":"러스트 언어 증명携带 데이터 프레임워크는 안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 데이터 처리 시스템을 구축하기 위한 도구입니다","es":"El marco de datos de prueba de Rust es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite implementar pruebas de datos de manera eficiente","fr":"Le cadre de données de preuve de langage Rust est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de mettre en œuvre des tests de données de manière efficace","de":"Das Rust-Sprachframework für Datenprüfung ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das die effiziente Implementierung von Datenprüfungen ermöglicht","pt":"O framework de dados de prova de Rust é uma tecnologia de IA que permite aos desenvolvedores criar aplicativos mais seguros e eficientes.","ru":"Фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust - это технология ИИ, которая позволяет разработчикам создавать более безопасные и эффективные приложения.","ar":"إطار بيانات لغة روست هو تكنولوجيا ذكاء اصطناعي يسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تطبيقات أكثر أمانًا وكفاءة.","en":"Rust language proof-carrying data framework"},"definition":{"en":"Rust language proof-carrying data framework"},"features":{"zh":["使用Rust语言构建","证明携带数据技术","提高数据处理安全性","增强开发效率","支持多种数据格式"],"ja":["Rust言語を使用して構築","プルーフキャリングデータ技術","データ処理の安全性を向上","開発効率を向上","多種のデータ形式をサポート"],"ko":["러스트 언어로 구축","증명携带 데이터 기술","데이터 처리 보안성 향상","개발 효율성 향상","다양한 데이터 형식 지원"],"es":["Implementación de pruebas de datos eficientes","Uso del lenguaje de programación Rust","Integración con herramientas de AI","Mejora de la seguridad y la confiabilidad de los datos","Flexibilidad y personalización para proyectos de desarrollo"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de tests de données efficaces","Utilisation du langage de programmation Rust","Intégration avec des outils d''IA","Amélioration de la sécurité et de la fiabilité des données","Flexibilité et personnalisation pour les projets de développement"],"de":["Effiziente Implementierung von Datenprüfungen","Verwendung der Programmiersprache Rust","Integration mit KI-Tools","Verbesserung der Sicherheit und Zuverlässigkeit von Daten","Flexibilität und Anpassungsfähigkeit für Entwicklungsprojekte"],"pt":["Segurança aprimorada com prova de dados","Desenvolvimento de aplicativos mais eficientes","Integração com linguagem Rust","Suporte a desenvolvedores","Documentação completa"],"ru":["Улучшенная безопасность с помощью носимых данных","Разработка более эффективных приложений","Интеграция с языком Rust","Поддержка разработчиков","Полная документация"],"ar":["أمان محسن مع بيانات البرهان","تطوير تطبيقات أكثر كفاءة","التكامل مع لغة روست","دعم المطورين","وثائق شاملة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust语言","证明携带数据框架","AI智能工具","数据处理安全","开发效率提高","如何使用Rust语言","什么是证明携带数据","Rust语言与AI","数据安全解决方案"],"ja":["Rust言語","プルーフキャリングデータフレームワーク","AIエージェント","データ処理の安全性","開発効率を向上","Rust言語の使い方","プルーフキャリングデータとは","Rust言語とAI","データセキュリティソリューション"],"ko":["러스트 언어","증명携带 데이터 프레임워크","AI 에이전트","데이터 처리 보안","개발 효율성 향상","러스트 언어 사용법","증명携带 데이터란","러스트 언어와 AI","데이터 보안 솔루션"],"es":["herramientas de AI","marco de datos de prueba de Rust","desarrollo de software","pruebas de datos","seguridad de datos","langage de programación Rust","alternativas a Rust","Rust vs otros lenguajes de programación","cómo usar Rust para pruebas de datos","guía de instalación de Rust"],"fr":["outils d''IA","cadre de données de preuve de langage Rust","développement de logiciels","tests de données","sécurité des données","langage de programmation Rust","alternatives à Rust","Rust vs autres langages de programmation","comment utiliser Rust pour les tests de données","guide d''installation de Rust"],"de":["KI-Tools","Rust-Sprachframework für Datenprüfung","Software-Entwicklung","Datenprüfungen","Datensicherheit","Programmiersprache Rust","Alternativen zu Rust","Rust vs andere Programmiersprachen","wie man Rust für Datenprüfungen verwendet","Installationsanleitung für Rust"],"pt":["como usar o framework de dados de prova de Rust","o que é o framework de dados de prova de Rust","framework de dados de prova de Rust alternative","Rust vs outros frameworks","instalar o framework de dados de prova de Rust","guia de configuração do framework de dados de prova de Rust","desenvolvimento de aplicativos com Rust","segurança de aplicativos com Rust"],"ru":["как использовать фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust","что такое фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust","фреймворк носимых данных языка Rust альтернатива","Rust vs другие фреймворки","установка фреймворка носимых данных языка Rust","руководство по настройке фреймворка носимых данных языка Rust","разработка приложений с помощью Rust","безопасность приложений с помощью Rust"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام إطار بيانات لغة روست","ما هو إطار بيانات لغة روست","إطار بيانات لغة روست بديل","روست مقابل إطارات أخرى","تثبيت إطار بيانات لغة روست","دليل إعداد إطار بيانات لغة روست","تطوير التطبيقات بلغة روست","أمان التطبيقات بلغة روست"]}},"owner":"tachyon-zcash","repo":"ragu","repoPath":"tachyon-zcash/ragu","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.895Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"book-review","description":"Review any part of the book using parallel specialist agents","bodyPreview":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:","body":"# Book Review\n\nReview part of the book specified by `$ARGUMENTS`, using the project''s book\nreview policies.\n\n## Step 1: Figure Out What to Review\n\nThe user''s `$ARGUMENTS` could be anything. Interpret them:\n\n| Arguments | What to do |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| *(empty)* | Run `git diff -- book/src/` and `git diff --cached -- book/src/`. Review the uncommitted changes. If no changes, say so and stop. |\n| A file path | Read that file. Review the whole chapter. |\n| A file path with lines (`foo.md:50-80`) | Read that file. Focus the review on those lines (but read the full file for context). |\n| Multiple file paths | Read all of them. Review each, and also look for consistency across them. |\n| A section heading or topic name | Use Grep/Glob to find where that topic is discussed in `book/src/`. Read those sections. Review them. |\n| A conceptual description (\"how we explain X\", \"the transition between Y and Z\") | Search the book to find the relevant passages. Read them with surrounding context. Review them as a unit. |\n| A mix of the above | Handle each part, then review the union. |\n\nIf you''re unsure what the user means, ask before launching reviewers.\n\n## Step 2: Discover and Launch Reviewers\n\n1. Use Glob to find all `.claude/book-review/*.md` files.\n2. Read `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards shared by all\n   reviewers).\n3. For EACH policy file **except `standards.md`**, launch a `general-purpose`\n   Task agent (use model `sonnet`). Give each agent a prompt constructed from\n   this template — adapt it based on what you''re reviewing:\n\n   > You are reviewing part of \"The Ragu Book,\" a technical book about a\n   > recursive proof system (proof-carrying data framework).\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards that always apply)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your specific review policy)\n   >\n   > **What to review:** {describe the specific content — file paths, line\n   > ranges, the topic, whatever the user specified. If reviewing a diff,\n   > include the diff text and list the full file paths for context.}\n   >\n   > {If the scope is a diff or a narrow range, add: \"Focus on the specified\n   > content. Flag issues in surrounding text ONLY if the specified content\n   > introduced an inconsistency with it.\"}\n   >\n   > {If the scope spans multiple files or a concept, add: \"Pay attention to\n   > consistency across the passages. Flag contradictions, redundancies, or\n   > gaps in the explanation as it spans these locations.\"}\n   >\n   > If the policy references other files (like `book/macros.txt` or\n   > `book/src/appendix/terminology.md`), read those too.\n   >\n   > For each finding:\n   > - **Location**: file path and quoted text (or line number)\n   > - **Issue**: what''s wrong, specifically\n   > - **Suggestion**: a concrete rewrite, not just \"improve this\"\n   > - **Severity**: `must-fix` (clearly wrong/confusing) or `suggestion`\n   >\n   > Stay within your policy''s scope. Be specific. If you find no real issues,\n   > say so — don''t manufacture problems.\n\n   Additionally, read `book/FIXME.md` and extract the `###`-level headings\n   under `## Deferred Issues`. Include them in each reviewer''s prompt as a\n   bullet list with the instruction:\n   > The following issues are already tracked and deferred. Do NOT raise\n   > findings that duplicate or overlap with these items. If your finding\n   > is essentially the same issue, omit it.\n   >\n   > {bullet list of ### headings from book/FIXME.md}\n   >\n   > However, if while reviewing you notice that a deferred issue appears to\n   > have been **resolved** by existing content or is now easily resolvable\n   > given changes in the surrounding text, mention it as a separate\n   > observation (not a finding). Format:\n   > - **Resolvable FIXME**: \"{FIXME heading}\" — {brief explanation of why\n   >   it appears resolved or how to resolve it now}\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel (multiple Task calls in one message).\n\n## Step 3: Run Automated Link Checks\n\nIn parallel with the reviewer agents (launched in Step 2), run the automated\nQA scripts to detect broken links and dead pages:\n\n1. Run `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py` — finds broken internal links and\n   invalid anchors (requires `mdbook` to be installed).\n2. Run `python3 qa/book/dead_pages.py` — finds markdown files not listed in\n   `SUMMARY.md`.\n3. Run `python3 qa/book/line_width.py` — finds lines exceeding the\n   80-character width limit (excludes code blocks, math blocks, and other\n   exempt content).\n\nIf either script fails to run (e.g., `mdbook` is not installed), note the\nfailure in your output but do not block the review. Include any findings from\nthese scripts alongside the reviewer agents'' results in the synthesis step.\n\n## Step 4: Synthesize\n\nOnce all agents return, organize findings by location (earliest in the book\nfirst). If multiple reviewers flagged overlapping concerns, merge them. Present:\n\n- **Must-fix** issues first\n- **Suggestions** second\n- For each finding, note which reviewer(s) identified it\n\nIf the review scope was cross-file or conceptual, add a short section at the end\nabout cross-cutting observations (consistency, narrative coherence, etc.).\n\nBefore presenting findings, read `book/FIXME.md` and remove any finding that\nsubstantially overlaps with an already-deferred issue (match against the `###`\nheadings). If you remove findings this way, do not mention them at all.\n\nIf any reviewer flagged a resolvable FIXME, collect them in a **Potentially\nResolvable FIXMEs** section after the main findings. The user can then use\n`/book-fixme` to address them.\n\n## Step 5: Validate Proposed Changes\n\nAfter synthesizing findings, but before presenting them to the user:\n\n1. Collect all proposed changes (the \"suggestion\" field from each finding) into\n   a single numbered list — the **proposed plan**.\n2. For EACH policy file (same set as Step 2 — every `.claude/book-review/*.md`\n   except `standards.md`), launch a `general-purpose` Task agent (model\n   `sonnet`) with this prompt:\n\n   > You are validating a set of proposed book edits against review policies.\n   >\n   > Read these files:\n   > - `.claude/book-review/standards.md` (master standards)\n   > - `.claude/book-review/{focus}.md` (your policy)\n   >\n   > Here is the proposed plan of changes:\n   > {numbered list of proposed changes with locations and suggested rewrites}\n   >\n   > For each proposed change, check whether applying it would **introduce** a\n   > violation of any rule in your policy or the master standards. Only flag\n   > real conflicts — do not restate rules that are already satisfied.\n   >\n   > For each conflict found:\n   > - **Change #**: which proposed change\n   > - **Rule violated**: quote the relevant policy text\n   > - **Conflict**: explain specifically how the suggestion violates the rule\n   > - **Resolution**: suggest how to fix the suggestion to comply\n   >\n   > If no proposed changes conflict with your policy, say so.\n\n   Launch ALL agents in parallel.\n\n3. Merge validation feedback into the findings. For each conflict:\n   - If the validator provides a compliant alternative, replace the original\n     suggestion with the corrected version.\n   - If the conflict has no clear resolution, annotate the finding with the\n     conflict so the user can decide during triage.\n\n4. If any suggestions were corrected, briefly note it in the synthesis output\n   (e.g., \"Grammar validator caught that suggestion #3 would violate the\n   lowercase-technical-terms rule; corrected.\").\n\n## Step 6: Triage\n\nAfter presenting findings, use AskUserQuestion to let the user decide the\ndisposition of each finding (or group of closely related findings). For each,\noffer:\n\n- **Fix** — apply the suggested fix now\n- **Skip** — drop this finding; do not record it anywhere\n- **Defer** — record this finding in `book/FIXME.md` for future attention\n\nIf there are many findings, you may batch them into logical groups and ask\nabout each group rather than each individual finding.\n\n## Step 7: Apply Fixes\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **fix**:\n\n1. Read the target file to get the current content.\n2. Apply the suggested change using the Edit tool. If the finding is a group\n   (e.g., \"add slugs to these 15 headings\"), apply all changes in the group.\n3. After applying all fixes, run any relevant QA scripts to verify the changes\n   don''t introduce new issues:\n   - If formatting changes were made: `python3 qa/book/line_width.py`\n   - If links or headings were changed: `python3 qa/book/broken_links.py`\n4. Briefly report what was changed and any QA results.\n\n## Step 8: Record Deferred Issues\n\nFor each finding the user chose to **defer**:\n\n1. Read `book/FIXME.md`.\n2. Check whether a substantially similar issue is already listed. First scan\n   the `###` headings for a potential match; if a heading looks similar, read\n   the paragraph beneath it to confirm it describes the same issue. Only skip\n   if both the heading and description match — do not treat a heading match\n   alone as a duplicate.\n3. If the issue is new, append it as a new `###`-level subsection under\n   `## Deferred Issues`, following the existing format: a short descriptive\n   heading, then a concise paragraph explaining the issue and its location.\n4. Write the updated file.\n\nAfter recording, confirm what was deferred and remind the user they can use\n`/book-refine` to turn feedback into policy improvements.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:10:41.343Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Language Agents like Claude Code or AutoGPT needing advanced text analysis capabilities for reviewing book content.","zh":"适合于 Claude Code 或 AutoGPT 等语言代理，需要高级文本分析功能来审阅书籍内容。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの言語エージェントに適しており、書籍コンテンツのレビューに高度なテキスト分析機能が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code 또는 AutoGPT 같은 언어 에이전트에 적합하며, 책 내용을 검토하기 위해 고급 텍스트 분석 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de lenguaje como Claude Code o AutoGPT que necesitan capacidades de análisis de texto avanzadas para revisar contenido de libros.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de langage comme Claude Code ou AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités d''analyse de texte avancées pour examiner le contenu de livres.","de":"Ideal für Sprachagenten wie Claude Code oder AutoGPT, die erweiterte Textanalysefunktionen zur Überprüfung von Buchinhalten benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem como Claude Code ou AutoGPT que precisam de capacidades avançadas de análise de texto para revisar conteúdo de livros.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, таких как Claude Code или AutoGPT, которые требуют расширенных возможностей анализа текста для просмотра содержания книг.","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة مثل Claude Code أو AutoGPT الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات分析 متقدمة للنص لمراجعة محتوى الكتب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to interpret and review book chapters using Git diff analysis, supporting review of uncommitted changes, specific file paths, and line ranges within files like ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizing Rust language proof-carrying data frameworks.","zh":"赋予代理审阅书籍章节的能力，使用 Git diff 分析，支持审阅未提交的更改、特定文件路径以及文件中的行范围，例如 ''foo.md:10-20''，利用 Rust 语言证明携带数据框架。","ja":"エージェントが書籍の章を解釈してレビューできるようにし、Git diff 分析を使用して、コミットされていない変更、特定のファイルパス、ファイル内の行範囲（例：''foo.md:10-20''）のレビューをサポートし、Rust 言語の証明付きデータフレームワークを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 책 章을 해석하고 검토할 수 있도록 하며, Git diff 분석을 사용하여 커밋되지 않은 변경 사항, 특정 파일 경로 및 파일 내의 줄 범위(''foo.md:10-20'' 예시)를 검토하도록 지원하며, Rust 언어 증명 携带 데이터 프레임워크를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a interpretar y revisar capítulos de libros utilizando el análisis de Git diff, lo que admite la revisión de cambios no confirmados, rutas de archivo específicas y rangos de líneas dentro de archivos como ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizando frameworks de datos de prueba de lenguaje Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''interpréter et d''examiner des chapitres de livres en utilisant l''analyse de Git diff, ce qui prend en charge l''examen des modifications non validées, des chemins de fichiers spécifiques et des plages de lignes à l''intérieur de fichiers comme ''foo.md:10-20'', en utilisant des frameworks de données de preuve de langage Rust.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Kapitel von Büchern mithilfe der Git-Diff-Analyse zu interpretieren und zu überprüfen, was die Überprüfung von nicht committeten Änderungen, spezifischer Dateipfade und Zeilenbereiche innerhalb von Dateien wie ''foo.md:10-20'' unterstützt, unter Verwendung von Rust-Sprachnachweisdatenframeworks.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a interpretar e revisar capítulos de livros usando análise Git diff, suportando revisão de alterações não comprometidas, caminhos de arquivo específicos e intervalos de linhas dentro de arquivos como ''foo.md:10-20'', utilizando frameworks de dados de prova de linguagem Rust.","ru":"Позволяет агентам интерпретировать и просматривать главы книг, используя анализ Git diff, поддерживая просмотр незафиксированных изменений, определенные пути файлов и диапазоны строк внутри файлов, таких как ''foo.md:10-20'', используя фреймворки языка Rust для переноса данных.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكيل من تفسير ومراجعة فصول الكتب باستخدام تحليل Git diff، مع دعم مراجعة التغييرات غير الملتزمة، مسارات الملفات المحددة، ونطاقات السطور داخل الملفات مثل ''foo.md:10-20''، باستخدام إطار العمل للغة روست لحمل البيانات."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing uncommitted book chapter changes","Analyzing specific file paths within a book project","Debugging line ranges in markdown files"],"zh":["审阅未提交的书籍章节更改","分析书籍项目中的特定文件路径","调试标记文件中的行范围"],"ja":["コミットされていない書籍章の変更のレビュー","書籍プロジェクト内の特定のファイルパスの分析","マークダウンファイル内の行範囲のデバッグ"],"ko":["커밋되지 않은 책 章 변경 사항 검토","책 프로젝트 내 특정 파일 경로 분석","마크다운 파일 내 줄 범위 디버깅"],"es":["Revisar cambios no confirmados de capítulos de libros","Analizar rutas de archivo específicas dentro de un proyecto de libro","Depurar rangos de líneas en archivos markdown"],"fr":["Examiner les modifications non validées des chapitres de livres","Analyser des chemins de fichiers spécifiques à l''intérieur d''un projet de livre","Déboguer des plages de lignes dans des fichiers markdown"],"de":["Überprüfen von nicht committeten Änderungen an Buchkapiteln","Analysieren von spezifischen Dateipfaden innerhalb eines Buchprojekts","Fehlerbehebung von Zeilenbereichen in Markdown-Dateien"],"pt":["Revisar alterações não comprometidas de capítulos de livros","Analizar caminhos de arquivo específicos dentro de um projeto de livro","Depurar intervalos de linhas em arquivos markdown"],"ru":["Просмотр незафиксированных изменений глав книг","Анализ определенных путей файлов внутри проекта книги","Отладка диапазонов строк в файлах markdown"],"ar":["مراجعة التغييرات غير الملتزمة لفصول الكتب","تحليل مسارات الملفات المحددة داخل مشروع كتاب","تصحيح أخطاء نطاقات السطور في ملفات ماركداون"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to reviewing content in ''book/src/'' directory","Needs Rust language proof-carrying data framework compatibility"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","仅限于 ''book/src/'' 目录内的内容审阅","需要 Rust 语言证明携带数据框架兼容性"],"ja":["Git のインストールと設定が必要","''book/src/'' ディレクトリ内のコンテンツのレビューのみ","Rust 言語の証明付きデータフレームワークとの互換性が必要"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성이 필요","''book/src/'' 디렉토리 내의 내용 검토만 가능","Rust 언어 증명携带 데이터 프레임워크와의 호환성이 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado a la revisión de contenido en el directorio ''book/src/''","Necesita compatibilidad con el framework de datos de prueba de lenguaje Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité à l''examen du contenu dans le répertoire ''book/src/''","Nécessite la compatibilité avec le framework de données de preuve de langage Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Überprüfung von Inhalten im Verzeichnis ''book/src/''","Benötigt Kompatibilität mit dem Rust-Sprachnachweisdatenframework"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado à revisão de conteúdo no diretório ''book/src/''","Necessita de compatibilidade com framework de dados de prova de linguagem Rust"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки Git","Ограничен просмотром содержания в директории ''book/src/''","Требует совместимости с фреймворком языка Rust для переноса данных"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين Git","محدود بمراجعة المحتوى في الدليل ''book/src/''","يحتاج إلى توافق مع إطار العمل للغة روست لحمل البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"03ecd3daf1c141683fc43f208d3e2aa567dcb6a2478d219704e3e6dbd58cc56e","qualityScore":24}');
